-# ---------------- Edit property partners modal ----------------
#pcEditModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title
          Edit Partners —
          %span#pcEditPropName
      .modal-body
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          Toggle which partner listing sites may display this property's Pynwheel interactive map.
        - Partner.registry.each do |p|
          .pc-toggle-row
            %span.pc-label= p.label
            .TriSea-technologies-Switch
              %span.pr-15 No
              = check_box_tag "pc_edit_#{p.key}", true, false, class: "pc-edit-toggle", data: { key: p.key }
              %label.label-primary{ for: "pc_edit_#{p.key}" }
              %span.pl-15 Yes
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-success#pcEditSave{ type: "button" } Save changes

-# ---------------- Delete (remove all) confirm modal ----------------
#pcDeleteModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog.modal-sm{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title
          %i.fa.fa-exclamation-triangle.text-danger.mr-10
          Remove partners
      .modal-body
        %p
          Remove
          %strong all partner assignments
          from
          %strong#pcDeletePropName
          ?
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          This property will no longer appear on any partner listing site's map. You can re-enable partners at any time.
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-danger#pcDeleteConfirm{ type: "button" } Remove all

-# ---------------- Bulk set-partners modal ----------------
#pcBulkModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title
          Set partners for
          %span#pcBulkCount
          selected
      .modal-body
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          Turn partners on or off, then Apply. The selected properties will be set to
          %strong exactly
          these partners — replacing whatever they currently have.
        - Partner.registry.each do |p|
          .pc-toggle-row
            %span.pc-label= p.label
            .TriSea-technologies-Switch
              %span.pr-15 No
              = check_box_tag "pc_bulk_#{p.key}", true, false, class: "pc-bulk-toggle", data: { key: p.key }
              %label.label-primary{ for: "pc_bulk_#{p.key}" }
              %span.pl-15 Yes
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-primary#pcBulkConfirm{ type: "button" } Apply to selected

-# ---------------- Add partner modal ----------------
-# Adding a partner is a row in the registry, so no deploy is needed to put the
-# next partner on this screen.
#pcAddPartnerModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title Add partner
      .modal-body
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          The partner gets its own tab here straight away. Generate its API key from
          that tab once you have agreed the property list.
        .form-group
          %label.control-label{ for: "pcPartnerLabel" } Display name
          = text_field_tag :pc_partner_label, nil, id: "pcPartnerLabel", class: "form-control", placeholder: "e.g. Jonah", autocomplete: "off"
          %span.help-block.font-size-12 Shown on the tab and on the property rows.
        .form-group
          %label.control-label{ for: "pcPartnerKey" } Identifier
          = text_field_tag :pc_partner_key, nil, id: "pcPartnerKey", class: "form-control", placeholder: "jonah", autocomplete: "off"
          %span.help-block.font-size-12
            Lowercase letters, numbers and underscores. Used in the API and in stored
            data, so it cannot be changed later.
        .pc-inline-error#pcAddPartnerError
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-primary#pcAddPartnerSave{ type: "button" } Add partner

-# ---------------- Rotate / generate key confirm ----------------
#pcRotateModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title
          %i.fa.fa-refresh.mr-10
          %span#pcRotateTitle Generate API key
      .modal-body
        %p#pcRotateBody
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          The key is shown once, on a link you can send to the partner. Pynwheel never
          stores a readable copy.
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-primary#pcRotateConfirm{ type: "button" } Generate

-# ---------------- One-time key link ----------------
#pcKeyLinkModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog", data: { backdrop: "static" } }
  .modal-dialog{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %h4.modal-title
          %i.fa.fa-key.mr-10
          Send this link to the partner
      .modal-body
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13#pcKeyLinkIntro
        .pc-copy-row
          = text_field_tag :pc_key_link, nil, id: "pcKeyLink", class: "form-control", readonly: true, onclick: "this.select();"
          %button.btn.btn-default#pcKeyLinkCopy{ type: "button", title: "Copy link" }
            %i.fa.fa-copy
        .pc-key-warning
          %i.fa.fa-exclamation-triangle.mr-5
          The link opens once and expires after 72 hours. Nobody — including Pynwheel —
          can read the key again afterwards; if it is lost, rotate to issue a new one.
      .modal-footer
        %a.btn.btn-default#pcKeyLinkEmail{ href: "#" }
          %i.fa.fa-envelope-o.mr-5
          Email to partner
        %button.btn.btn-primary{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Done

-# ---------------- Revoke key confirm ----------------
#pcRevokeModal.modal.fade{ tabindex: "-1", role: "dialog" }
  .modal-dialog.modal-sm{ role: "document" }
    .modal-content
      .modal-header
        %button.close{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } }
          %span &times;
        %h4.modal-title
          %i.fa.fa-ban.text-danger.mr-10
          Revoke API key
      .modal-body
        %p
          Revoke
          %strong#pcRevokePartnerName
          's API key?
        %p.text-muted.font-size-13
          Their API requests start failing immediately. The property associations are
          kept, so issuing a new key puts them straight back in business.
      .modal-footer
        %button.btn.btn-default{ type: "button", data: { dismiss: "modal" } } Cancel
        %button.btn.btn-danger#pcRevokeConfirm{ type: "button" } Revoke key
